\par \f1\b\fs28 8. Termination\par 
\f0\b0\fs24 
\par 
\par \f1\b\fs24 8.1 By you\par 
\f0\b0\fs24 
\par 
You may stop using Hippocampus at any time. To fully terminate:\par 
\par 
1. Quit Hippocampus.\par 
2. Delete the Hippocampus.app application bundle.\par 
3. Delete ~/Library/Application Support/MCI/ (your brain database and blobs).\par 
4. Optionally delete ~/Library/Logs/MCI/ (local crash and health logs).\par 
\par 
No account closure is needed because no account exists for the local product.\par 
\par 
\par \f1\b\fs24 8.2 By us\par 
\f0\b0\fs24 
\par 
We may terminate or suspend your access to the Software if you violate these Terms. For the local product, "termination" means we may revoke your license to use the Software \u8212? but because your data is local and encrypted with a key we do not hold, we cannot delete or access your data.\par 
\par 
For Hippocampus for Teams, termination of a subscription means the workspace server stops serving sync requests. Your local data remains on your device.\par 
\par 
\par \f1\b\fs24 8.3 Effect of termination\par 
\f0\b0\fs24 
